# Stub for a Dart-snapshot import this fork does not have.
#
# Upstream, `flutter/shell/platform/android/BUILD.gn` imports this file to name
# the Dart AOT/JIT snapshot binaries it builds and links. This fork has no Dart
# VM: `flutter/lib/snapshot/` was never tracked (there is no `dart:` directory,
# no `packages/`, no Dart SDK in DEPS), so the import cannot resolve -- and GN
# loads a BUILD.gn file whole, so *every* target in
# `flutter/shell/platform/android/BUILD.gn` fails to load with the file simply
# absent. That is not a hypothetical: depending on
# `//flutter/shell/platform/android:flutter_shell_native_src` -- which is where
# `PlatformViewAndroid`, `PlatformViewAndroidJNIImpl` and
# `SurfaceTextureExternalTextureGLImpeller` live, and which the video texture
# path reuses verbatim -- failed `gn gen` twice on exactly this.
#
# The stub defines nothing, which is correct rather than lazy: the targets this
# fork actually builds reference none of the snapshot variables, so an empty file
# lets GN parse the BUILD.gn and leaves every Dart-dependent target (snapshot,
# isolate, flutter_patched_sdk) undefined for anyone who tries to build one.
#
# If a Dart-dependent target is ever needed here, this stub has to be replaced
# with the real gen_snapshot.gni and the Dart subtree restored -- it is a record
# of what is missing, not a way around it.

declare_args() {
  # Present so any target that does read an argument still parses; see above.
  rustflutter_no_dart_snapshot = true
}